			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Migrate to Effect-TS native architecture and remove legacy Bootstrap\n\nThis commit represents a major architectural refactoring of the `Wind` UI service layer, moving away from imperative TypeScript classes and legacy bootstrapping logic to a fully declarative, Effect-TS-based architecture.\n\nKey changes include:\n\n1.  **Legacy Deletion:** Removed the extensive `Source/Bootstrap` directory structure (Core, Stages, Integration) and `Source/Desktop` services (TauriConfigurationService, TauriFileService, etc.). These have been replaced by composable Effect services.\n\n2.  **New Effect Services:** Introduced core services within `Source/Effect/` to handle application lifecycle:\n    -   `Bootstrap`: Orchestrates startup stages (Environment, Preload, Configuration, Services, Initialization, HealthCheck) using Effect sequencing.\n    -   `Environment`: Provides platform detection and environment info (formerly Stage 0).\n    -   `Health`: Monitors service availability and system health (formerly Stage 6).\n    -   `MountainSync`: Manages state synchronization between `Wind` and `Mountain` using reactive streams.\n    -   `Clipboard`: Migrated from `Source/Application` to `Source/Effect` with full Effect-TS error handling.\n\n3.  **Dependency Management:** Added `effect` and `effect-website` as submodules in `Module/`, aligning with the project's commitment to Effect-TS for all application logic.\n\n4.  **Build System:** Updated ESBuild configurations (`Configuration/ESBuild/Target.js`, `Compile.js`, `Wind.js`) to minify output in production and correctly handle the new file structure.\n\nThis refactoring consolidates the logic previously scattered across multiple classes and stages into a unified, dependency-injected `Layer` architecture, significantly improving testability, composability, and type safety.",
			"SHA": "6bfd8cd7daaefc2b7f1010b9cf54ab7034cd39cb"
		},
